    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` feature so the application flags a city approaching its per-city capacity limit.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new read-only boolean `capacityWarning` property to the Owner schema (the DTO is code-generated from this spec at build time), documented as true when the owner's city holds 40\u201349 owners.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constant.\n   - Added an `isApproachingCityCapacity(city)` helper that reuses the existing `countOwnersInCity` and returns true when the count is in `[40, 50)` (i.e. `>= 40 && < CITY_OWNER_LIMIT`).\n   - Set `capacityWarning` on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response (the path the test asserts on) and, for consistency, on the create response \u2014 mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern.\n\nThe hard rejection at 50 (`OwnerCityFullException` in `enforceCreateLimits`) is untouched, and the warning window (40\u201349) is strictly below it.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` \u2014 and the full suite \u2014 pass: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
